<Base title="Accordion" description="One or more Tile disclosures coordinated into a single framework.">
  <h1>Accordion</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The root coordinates disclosure tiles and gives them a shared framework. Each item remains a <code>sk-tile--expandable</code>: a single interaction in the trigger. Choose <code>single</code> for an open section or <code>multiple</code> for independent disclosures.
  </p>

  <p>
    If the state can live in HTML and a native exclusive group is sufficient, see <a href="#native-details">Native details</a> at the end. Accordion is the primary route when you need controlled coordination, <code>multiple</code>, or change events.
  </p>

  <h2>One item</h2>
  <p>
    For an isolated disclosure (formerly “ExpandableTile”), use Accordion with a single item: the root provides the frame and the Tile retains the surface and state layer.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview html={single} label="Accordion of an item">
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <AccordionSingleDemo client:load />
    </Fragment>
  </ComponentPreview>

  <h2>Exclusive group</h2>
  <p>
    <code>data-type="single"</code> in HTML, <code>type="single"</code> in React, keeps at most one item open. With <code>data-collapsible="false"</code> or <code>collapsible={false}</code>, the open item cannot be closed.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview html={exclusive} label="Accordion single">
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <AccordionExclusiveDemo client:load />
    </Fragment>
  </ComponentPreview>

  <h2>Multigroup</h2>
  <p><code>type="multiple"</code> maintains each disclosure independently.</p>
  <ComponentPreview html={multiple} react={react} label="Accordion multiple">
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <AccordionMultipleDemo client:load />
    </Fragment>
  </ComponentPreview>

  <h2>Vanilla</h2>
  <p>
    The enhancer mounts the root <code>data-sk-accordion</code> and adds <code>sk-accordion</code>. Each direct child declares <code>data-part="item"</code> and a unique <code>data-value</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={vanilla} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>Contract</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The root is authored with <code>data-sk-accordion</code> (and optionally <code>class="sk-accordion"</code> in static HTML). The enhancer writes <code>data-part="root"</code> and the class <code>sk-accordion</code>.</li>
    <li><code>sk-accordion</code> joins the items into a single frame; each direct item <code>sk-tile sk-tile--interactive sk-tile--expandable</code> preserves anatomy and state layer without its own border.</li>
    <li>A direct item uses <code>sk-tile sk-tile--interactive sk-tile--expandable</code>, <code>data-part="item"</code>, and a single <code>data-value</code>.</li>
    <li>Trigger and content retain the native Tile parts: <code>trigger</code> and <code>content</code>.</li>
    <li>Opening an item does not paint the selection border: that is for checkbox and radio.</li>
    <li>In <code>single</code>, <code>data-collapsible="false"</code> or <code>collapsible={false}</code> leave the chosen item open. In <code>multiple</code> that option does not apply.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="native-details">Native details</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code> are already an accessible platform disclosure. Share a <code>name</code> attribute between siblings so that the browser keeps a single item open: a native accordion, without machine or <code>@skryensya/vanilla</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use when the state can live in the document. Choose Accordion enhanced when you need controlled value, <code>multiple</code>, change callbacks, or composition with system events. The Tile anatomy (title, description, chevron) is the same, so the group looks the same.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview html={nativeDetails} label="Details with shared name" />

  <h3>Install only Details</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={nativeInstall} label="terminal" />
  <CodeBlock code={nativeStyles} label="CSS" lang="css" />

  <h3>Native contract</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The first interactive child of each <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> is its <code>&lt;summary&gt;</code>.</li>
    <li>The <code>open</code> attribute declares the initial state in HTML.</li>
    <li>The same <code>name</code> between siblings makes the group exclusive; without <code>name</code>, each disclosure is independent.</li>
    <li>Browser changes <code>open</code>; there is no controlled value or system event to listen to.</li>
  </ul>

  <StylingHooks groups={[{ file: "components/details.css", probe: "sk-details" }]} />
</Base>
